==English==

===Etymology===
1923, coined by American cartoonist [[w:Billy_De_Beck|Billy De Beck]] in his comic strip [[w:Barney_Google|Barney Google]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhiː.biːˌdʒiː.biːz/}}, {{SAMPA|/"hi:.bi:%dZi.bi:z/}}

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun}}

# {{US|idiomatic}} A general feeling of [[anxiety]], [[fear]], [[uneasiness]], or [[nausea]].
#:''I don't mind worms, but spiders give me the '''heebie-jeebies'''.''

